      "content": "That makes sense. Looking at the data for the specific Westside district, the influx is primarily from South Asian and East African communities. \n\nIn your experience analyzing similar urban shifts, do these specific demographic profiles tend to correlate with higher or lower \"social volatility\" scores compared to, say, a white-majority demographic shift? I'm trying to see if there are statistical tendencies in how these specific ethnic/cultural groups impact local crime rates or neighborhood cohesion that we should account for in the volatility model.",
